{"id":"kumano-kodo","title":"Kumano Kodo: the Nakahechi","who":"Classic route · Japan's imperial pilgrimage, a sister trail of the Camino","when":"March–May and October–November","vehicle":"On foot, 4–5 days, family inns (minshuku)","kind":"walk","color":"#be123c","summary":"The emperors' old pilgrimage route through the forested mountains of the Kii peninsula to the three Grand Shrines of Kumano: stone paths under cedars, small oji shrines, hot springs at night and dinners in family inns. Walkers of both this and the Camino de Santiago can become \"dual pilgrims\".","sources":[{"label":"Camino forum: Kumano Kodo Nakahechi trip report (June 2026)","url":"https://www.caminodesantiago.me/community/threads/kumano-kodo-nakahechi-route-trip-report-june-2026.97252/"},{"label":"Third Eye Mom: Chikatsuyu to Hongu (October 2025)","url":"https://thirdeyemom.com/2025/10/21/hiking-the-kumano-kodo-nakahechi-trail-chikatsuyu-to-hongu-grand-shrine/"},{"label":"Ski Kangae: Kumano Kodo day 1 (March 2025)","url":"https://skikangae.blogspot.com/2025/03/kumano-kodo-day-1.html"}],"approximate":"The usual stages; the line follows paths near the waymarked trail.","km":106,"bbox":[135.3843,33.6684,135.8905,33.8617],"stops":[{"name":"Kii-Tanabe","place":"Kii-Tanabe Station","at":[33.7329,135.3845],"text":"The coastal town where pilgrims gather; a bus to the trailhead.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Tanabe_Montage.jpg/500px-Tanabe_Montage.jpg","page":"Tanabe, Wakayama","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tanabe_Montage.jpg","credit":"水だらけのプール","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Takijiri-oji","place":"Takijiri-oji","at":[33.7755,135.5037],"text":"The traditional entrance to the sacred mountains, and a steep first climb.","by":"bus","source":{"label":"Ski Kangae: day 1 (2025)","url":"https://skikangae.blogspot.com/2025/03/kumano-kodo-day-1.html"}},{"name":"Takahara","place":"Takahara, Tanabe","at":[33.7943,135.5293],"text":"A hilltop village called \"the village in the mist\", looking over the mountains.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Map_Kumano_Kodo.png/500px-Map_Kumano_Kodo.png","page":"Kumano Kodō","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Kumano_Kodo.png","credit":"ja:利用者: Yosemite","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Chikatsuyu","place":"Chikatsuyu, Tanabe","at":[33.7799,135.5885],"text":"A river village of minshuku inns: the end of the first day, about 13 km."},{"name":"Hosshinmon-oji","place":"Hosshinmon-oji","at":[33.8618,135.7208],"text":"The longest day, through forest and tea fields to the \"gate of awakening\".","source":{"label":"Third Eye Mom (2025)","url":"https://thirdeyemom.com/2025/10/21/hiking-the-kumano-kodo-nakahechi-trail-chikatsuyu-to-hongu-grand-shrine/"}},{"name":"Kumano Hongu Taisha","place":"Kumano Hongu Taisha","at":[33.8404,135.7736],"text":"The first Grand Shrine, and the giant torii gate at Oyunohara.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Shrine_Kumano_hongu_torii01.jpg/500px-Shrine_Kumano_hongu_torii01.jpg","page":"Kumano Hongū Taisha","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shrine_Kumano_hongu_torii01.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Yunomine Onsen","place":"Yunomine Onsen","at":[33.8288,135.7576],"text":"One of Japan's oldest hot springs, with a tiny bath carved in the river rock.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Kumano_Kodo_pilgrimage_route_Yunomine_Onsen_World_heritage_%E7%86%8A%E9%87%8E%E5%8F%A4%E9%81%93_%E6%B9%AF%E3%81%AE%E5%B3%B0%E6%B8%A9%E6%B3%8956.JPG/500px-Kumano_Kodo_pilgrimage_route_Yunomine_Onsen_World_heritage_%E7%86%8A%E9%87%8E%E5%8F%A4%E9%81%93_%E6%B9%AF%E3%81%AE%E5%B3%B0%E6%B8%A9%E6%B3%8956.JPG","page":"Yunomine Onsen","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kumano_Kodo_pilgrimage_route_Yunomine_Onsen_World_heritage_%E7%86%8A%E9%87%8E%E5%8F%A4%E9%81%93_%E6%B9